You will need to restore the original source. I got it as a tgz from
freshmeat.net (indirectly). the 3.43 version source is available at: 

http://www.nethack.org/v343/download-src.html

the precompiled windows (read dos) version is from:

http://www.nethack.org/v343/ports/download

this runs in everything from 95 up to XP

I would only worry about the source code if you are running a version of
*nix that it's not ported to yet or you have build your "distribution"
from packages off the net as opposed to buying a slackware etc. CD set. 

Did you try to do the compilation with the original sources as it says
in sys/msdos/Install.dos. You're obviously doing a dos compile as
opposed to the gui if you need ncurses. The dos version used DJGPP to
compile and used  to used microsoft C, but I guess that's been abandoned
(hard to say by who first ;-). I'm pretty sure Cygwin is only used for
the gui (read QT library version) of nethack. 

  All you really have to do is modify the .h files mentioned before you
  compile - never modify the source unless you have written a bigger
  program recently - things get bad *very* quickly that way. 

